Z||000009||Master_Sushi||10-03-2001||08:47 PM||||Well I wanted to get about 3500 for it. I sold it for about $3000. I have put allot of money into the car. But with almost any car you don't get back what you put into them. Ya it is in great shape. Most people would not believe me when I told them it was an 88. No I didn't want to sell it, but I basically had to. Cars come and go though.<P>I will be driving a black 84 se this winter. Should be fun as it has 16-inch berretta wheels/tires on it. It’s mostly to commute to and from work/college. Its funny I NEVER would have thought I'd be selling my pride and joy fiero and be driving my black fiero. I bought it several months ago as a parts car... lol <P>I like Fieros because they are fun, somewhat rare now and they look way faster then they really are  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. Almost complete opposite of a ricer. 0-60 isn't everything for a sports car either.||||reg||1
Z||000010||AutoXdbdragSE||10-04-2001||01:00 AM||||Guy's lets face reality, even the quickest fieros aren't that fast in stock trim.. the average import/domestic car now and days will give any fiero a run for it's money right up to it's speed limiter..  i realize i only own a 84SE with the muncie 4.10 so i'm not a fiero "speed" expert.. but yeah, there isn't much out there that can sprint to 30 as fast as my car, but 0-60.. my 9.2 is slow.. 8.6 is slow.. and 7.6 isn't exactly fast.. i think a toyota camry is 7.2ish.. so guys, lets face reality.. unmodde fieros aren't quick, fun HELL YES.  great handling cars.. ANOTHER HELL YES.. but quick by todays standards.. sadly no.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Fformula88||10-04-2001||10:18 AM||||Your right, even v6 Fieros aren't the quickest cars on the road.  However, I would rather take 15 seconds to get to 60 in a good looking sports car than have the quickest Camry ever built!<P>Speed isn't everything for Sports cars.  MG's are regarded as great sports cars, they were not that fast.  Even Miata's today only hit 60 in the 7's, and it doesn't have the excuse of being a 14-18 yr/old design!  <P>But don't get me wrong, I would love for a really fast Fiero!  But speed isn't why I own it.||||reg||1
Z||000012||falconhulk||10-04-2001||03:20 PM||||8 seconds is plenty fast!  It may not snap your neck but it does push you back into your seat.  I have a 85 Se V6 auto mildly modded with 54000 miles on it and it runs 0 to 60 in 8  to 8.3 seconds.  It feels a lot faster then that though.  This is a respectable time.||||reg||1
Z||000013||BN Boomer||10-04-2001||04:14 PM||||I just bought a new Impala LS with the 200hp 3.8 V6. It does 0-60 in something like 8.5 seconds, handles great, has excellent brakes, and looks awesome. AND has a backseat and a HUGE trunk.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I guess most of you guys are single kids who have no appreciation for a nice sedan. Don't worry, though, your day is coming.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
